!! Field aliases

<$reveal type="match" state="$:/config/rimir/namespace/field-aliases" text="no" default="no">
//Feature disabled — enable in Feature flags above.//
</$reveal>
<$reveal type="nomatch" state="$:/config/rimir/namespace/field-aliases" text="no" default="no">
Target-attached aliases — a tiddler T whose configured field lists
`Foo [[Foo Bar]] Old` will be the target of `[[Foo]]`, `[[Foo Bar]]`, and
`[[Old]]` references from anywhere. The field defaults to `aliases`;
override below.

''Alias field name:'' <$edit-text tiddler="$:/config/rimir/namespace/alias-field" default="aliases" tag="input" size="20"/>

''Tiddlers declaring aliases:''

<$list filter="[all[tiddlers+shadows]has{$:/config/rimir/namespace/alias-field}!is[system]] +[sort[]]" emptyMessage="<em>none defined</em>">
* <$link to=<<currentTiddler>>/> — <code><$view field={{$:/config/rimir/namespace/alias-field}}/></code>
</$list>

''Ambiguity report:''

<$list filter="[ns-field-alias-ambiguities[]]" variable="amb" emptyMessage="<em>no collisions — all alias tokens are unique</em>">
* <code><<amb>></code> — defined on:
<$list filter="[<amb>ns-field-alias-candidates[]]">
** <$link to=<<currentTiddler>>/>
</$list>
</$list>

To resolve a collision: remove the colliding token from the
`{{$:/config/rimir/namespace/alias-field}}` field on all but one of the
listed tiddlers. The remaining tiddler becomes the unique target for
that token.

In ''Restricted'' scope mode the resolver applies //locality narrowing//:
when a token is ambiguous globally but only ONE candidate lives in the
source's subtree, the link still works (it navigates to the local pick)
and the wider collision surfaces through the link's hover tooltip and a
`·` marker. So the report above is the //global// view; from any given
source the practical behaviour may be a working link with a hint.
</$reveal>

!! Mount points

Tiddlers tagged `$:/tags/NamespaceMount` with `from` + `to`.

<$list filter="[all[tiddlers+shadows]tag[$:/tags/NamespaceMount]]" emptyMessage="<em>none defined</em>">
* <code><$view field="from"/></code> → <code><$view field="to"/></code> &nbsp;<span style="opacity:0.7;">(<$link to=<<currentTiddler>>>source</$link>)</span>
</$list>

!! Diagnostic filters

These operators are exposed for scripting / debugging:

* `[<ref>ns-resolve<source>]` — resolve a single ref as if from `<source>`
* `[<ref>ns-resolve-class<source>]` — CSS class (`ns-resolved` / `ns-unresolved`)
* `[<title>ns-backlinks[]]` — sources that reference `<title>`
* `[<title>ns-forwardlinks[]]` — targets `<title>` references

Tiddler info sidebar includes a ''NS Backlinks'' tab showing the reverse
index for the current tiddler.
